s1-p18 : Block
s1-p18 = prose (cons "An utterance is a particularly direct instance. A participant produces an expression in one state; another receives it in a different state, interprets it, and responds. The interaction becomes part of the context of later expressions. What an expression means in this interaction therefore depends on the receiving participant, the retained history, and the interpretation in use. The account concerns those relationships, rather than a context-independent semantic payload imagined to travel inside the utterance. The study of conventions, language use, and symbolic grounding supplies relevant antecedents ([48](#ref-48)–[51](#ref-51)); here the participating interpreter is itself an evolving construction." nil)
